WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:04.259
Samwell Tarly: According to legend, House
Targaryen survived the Doom of Valyria thanks

00:00:04.259 --> 00:00:09.820
to Daenys the Dreamer, who foresaw the calamity
and convinced her father to flee their homeland.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:15.260
It could be true. The Targaryens were always
a bit more.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:22.080
Viserys Targaryen: This world wasn't always
so small and petty. Thousands of years ago,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:28.160
while the rest of men prayed to gods, the
Valyrians became them.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:34.850
Through magic or sheer will, they mastered
the greatest creatures in history. A horse

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:43.360
grants man dominion over the land, a ship
over the sea. But dragons gave us the sky,

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.960
and everything and everyone beneath it.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:53.980
At its height, my ancestors ruled the Known
World. Whatever parts we didn't weren't worth

00:00:53.980 --> 00:01:00.660
knowing. Our capital of Valyria shamed the
magnificent cities of the east, for hammers

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:08.670
and chisels were no match for dragonfire and
sorcery. It was a city and an empire built

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:15.790
to last until the end of time.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:16.790
It didn't.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.180
Four hundred years ago, the Doom fell on Valyria.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:24.340
Mountains cracked open like eggs. Lakes and
rivers boiled. Fountains of fire, ash, and

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:34.060
smoke spewed from the ground, so high and
so hot that even dragons burned in flight.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:40.770
The land splintered, and the angry sea rushed
in. In hours, the greatest city in history

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.080
became history.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:48.869
But my ancestors didn't burn or drown with
the rest of their race. Twelve years before

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:55.810
the Doom, despite the sneers of his rivals,
Aenar Targaryen abandoned the capital with

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.970
his family.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:03.979
Legends claim that his daughter foresaw the
destruction of the city in a dream. More likely,

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:09.380
Aenar met with some mishap at court and chose
exile over execution.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:19.720
He and House Targaryen slinked away to a dreary,
remote, godforsaken island. Forsaken no longer.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:26.959
With arts now lost to the world, we transformed
a tiny outpost into Dragonstone, a fortress

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:30.299
fit for the last Dragonlords.

00:02:30.299 --> 00:02:38.730
Then Aenar's descendants settled into it like
a tomb for their lost homeland. Until Aegon.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:48.169
When he looked east, he saw the past: old,
tired, dead. But when he looked west, he saw

00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:57.299
the future: gold in the ground, gold in the
fields, and no dragons in the sky but his.

00:02:57.299 --> 00:03:03.419
He and his sisters, Rhaenys and Visenya, flew
over the great continent, ostensibly visitors

00:03:03.419 --> 00:03:10.409
to a strange land. But when Aegon returned,
he ordered construction of a massive table

00:03:10.409 --> 00:03:14.959
carved in the shape of Westeros, with all
the notable rivers and mountains that they

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:24.739
had seen. A personal map of the Seven Kingdoms,
then ruled by seven squabbling families.

00:03:24.739 --> 00:03:31.959
House Durrandon held the Stormlands from their
seat at Storm's End, due south of Dragonstone.

00:03:31.959 --> 00:03:37.359
House Hoare of the Iron Islands had also conquered
and enslaved the Riverlands, and ruled them

00:03:37.359 --> 00:03:43.319
from Harrenhal, a monstrous castle rising
on the shore of the Gods Eye.

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:49.319
House Stark held the frozen wasteland of the
North, the oldest, largest, and emptiest of

00:03:49.319 --> 00:03:50.319
the kingdoms.

00:03:50.319 --> 00:03:56.469
House Lannister held the Westerlands, the
wealthiest kingdom thanks to their gold mines.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:04:01.620
House Gardener held the Reach, the second
wealthiest kingdom thanks to their crops.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:07.730
House Arryn held the Vale, or rather the Vale
held them. The mountains were impassable except

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:11.169
through the Bloody Gate, which had never been
taken.

00:04:11.169 --> 00:04:16.989
House Martell held the deserts of Dorne, probably
because no one else wanted them.

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:23.159
Together, the Seven Kingdoms made Westeros,
a realm that wasn't yet a realm, ruled by

00:04:23.159 --> 00:04:29.560
great families who didn't know what greatness
was. Aegon would teach them.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:36.539
Varys: Though House Durrandon titled themselves
"Storm Kings," they were little more than

00:04:36.539 --> 00:04:41.229
gusts. Their kingdom in the Stormlands had
been doddering to its end for the past few

00:04:41.229 --> 00:04:46.880
centuries, helped along by other houses. Most
of all by House Hoare, who were nearly finished

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:52.620
with a monstrous castle at Harrenhal, too
large and too costly a seat to rule only the

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.080
Riverlands.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:59.340
King Argilac knew where the Ironborn would
soon turn. You'd think a king who wanted to

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:04.419
keep his crown would be wary of a man with
fire-breathing monsters, but King Argilac

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:10.099
Durrandon wasn't called "the Arrogant" for
nothing. Determined to arrest decline, he

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:15.979
sent an envoy to Dragonstone to enlist Aegon
Targaryen and his dragons against his enemies.

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:22.590
In exchange, Argilac offered lands he didn't
have, and a wife Aegon didn't need. For as

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:28.960
the Valyrians did, Aegon had wed his elder
sister Visenya. Then as the Valyrians didn't,

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:37.040
he took the younger Rhaenys as well. Two sisters,
two wives. Perhaps that's why he was so keen

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.849
to get off Dragonstone.

00:05:38.849 --> 00:05:44.099
Aegon countered Argilac with courtesy. He
sent his own envoy requesting that Princess

00:05:44.099 --> 00:05:50.090
Durrandon's hand be given instead to Aegon's
closest friend and rumored half-brother, Orys

00:06:02.997 --> 00:06:09.788
been waiting for such a pretext? As his army
prepared to sail, ravens flew to every great

00:06:09.788 --> 00:06:15.217
lord of the Seven Kingdoms. All bore the same
message: From this day forth, there would

00:06:15.217 --> 00:06:20.938
be but one king in Westeros. Those who bent
the knee to Aegon of House Targaryen would

00:06:20.938 --> 00:06:26.677
keep their lands and titles. Those who took
up arms against him would be thrown down,

00:06:26.677 --> 00:06:34.178
humbled and destroyed. Poor old Argilac. He
couldn't even match Aegon in arrogance.

00:06:34.178 --> 00:06:39.047
Aegon landed at the mouth of the Blackwater
River and raised a primitive Aegonfort in

00:06:39.047 --> 00:06:43.908
the disputed lands between Harren's and Argilac's
kingdom so that neither could decide whose

00:06:43.908 --> 00:06:50.448
problem he was. Adopting the customs of the
Seven Kingdoms, Aegon unfurled his own banner

00:06:50.448 --> 00:06:56.108
with a red three-headed dragon breathing fire
upon a black field. Visenya crowned him with

00:06:56.108 --> 00:07:01.897
a ruby-studded circlet of Valyrian steel while
Rhaenys hailed him as the first high king

00:07:01.897 --> 00:07:07.538
the continent had seen since the Dawn Age.
As his lords and the gathered locals cheered

00:07:07.538 --> 00:07:14.397
him, Aegon named his loyal friends to a Small
Council led by Orys Baratheon, whom he called

00:07:21.515 --> 00:07:27.696
But for now, Aegon's kingdom contained only
a rocky island and a handful of fields. The

00:07:27.696 --> 00:07:33.256
other kings had large armies, ships, castles,
and thousands of years of rule. But Aegon

00:07:33.256 --> 00:07:40.835
had dragons. He had chosen for the words of
his house, "Fire and Blood." Before he was

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:45.066
done, the rivers, fields, and skies would
turn red.

00:07:45.066 --> 00:07:52.256
Euron Greyjoy: Harren of House Hoare inherited
a kingdom that stretched from the Iron Islands

00:07:52.256 --> 00:07:58.876
to the Trident. Too great a kingdom to rule
from a castle as shit as Pyke.

00:07:58.876 --> 00:08:05.286
For forty years, his ironborn plundered the
Riverlands for stone, timber, and slaves to

00:08:05.286 --> 00:08:12.886
build a seat worthy of him. Legend has it
that masons laid the final stone in Harrenhal

00:08:12.886 --> 00:08:16.916
on the very day that Aegon landed in Westeros.

00:08:23.582 --> 00:08:31.063
got there. They weren't the only ones. At
Aegon's approach, Harren's riverlords revolted,

00:08:31.063 --> 00:08:32.573
led by House Tully.

00:08:32.573 --> 00:08:35.732
I doubt Harren noticed.

00:08:35.732 --> 00:08:42.503
Harrenhal could repel an army of a million
men. No ladder could summit its walls, and

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:54.200
shut his gates around himself, his sons and
his ironborn, and waited for Aegon's army

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.390
to drain back into the muck.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:05.589
When Aegon finally saw the monstrous castle,
he asked for parley. Harren granted it. Valyria

00:09:05.589 --> 00:09:12.980
had been the greatest empire the world had
ever seen. Harren wanted to piss on its ashes.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:19.089
Viserys Targaryen: (as Aegon) "Yield now,
and you may remain Lord of the Iron Islands.

00:09:19.089 --> 00:09:27.080
Yield now, and your sons will live to rule
after you. You see my army outside your walls.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.620
You see my dragons."

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:34.980
Euron: (as Harren) "What is outside my walls
is of no concern. Those walls are strong and

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:35.980
thick."

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:38.469
Viserys: (as Aegon) "Dragons fly."

00:09:38.469 --> 00:09:42.540
Euron: (as Harren) "But stone doesn't burn."

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:48.230
Viserys: (as Aegon) "When the sun sets, your
line shall end."

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:54.130
Euron: Harren spat and returned to his castle.
Once inside, he promised lands, riches, and

00:09:54.130 --> 00:10:00.610
Tully's daughters to whoever could bring down
Aegon or his dragon. As the sun sank below

00:10:00.610 --> 00:10:07.579
the horizon, all Harren's men patrolled the
battlements, hearing wings in every gust of

00:10:07.579 --> 00:10:14.110
wind. But the moon rose and sank, and no dragon
appeared.

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:19.430
Viserys: While the ironborn were ringing the
battlements, Aegon drove his dragon Balerion

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:23.909
higher and higher in the night sky, so that
even the great castle of Harrenhal looked

00:10:23.909 --> 00:10:29.310
like an anthill below them. Then they plunged
straight into the castle, well inside the

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.070
guarded walls.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:36.870
The five towers of Harrenhal reached towards
Aegon like a hand. Balerion opened his mouth

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:39.450
and bathed all the fingers in flame.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:49.209
Euron: Harren was right. Stone doesn't burn,
but men do, even when they're ironborn. The

00:10:49.209 --> 00:10:55.630
dragon blasted my ancestors into ash that
choked the survivors when they screamed. Harren's

00:10:55.630 --> 00:11:03.329
soldiers leapt from the battlements and died.
They huddled against the walls and died. They

00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:05.550
fled across the yard and died.

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:13.839
Harren and his sons took shelter inside the
castle. The stone didn't burn, but as Balerion

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:19.829
blasted it with fire, it glowed white-hot.

00:11:19.829 --> 00:11:27.260
The world's greatest castle became the world's
greatest oven, baking the last of House Hoare

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:28.420
within it.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:34.300
Viserys: Outside the castle walls, the towers
of Harrenhal glowed red against the night

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:39.750
and began to twist and melt like five huge
candles, with liquid stone trickling down

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.490
their sides like wax.

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:48.959
The next morning, Aegon forged a new Riverlands.
He named the rebel Edmyn Tully as his Lord

00:11:48.959 --> 00:11:54.349
Paramount of the Trident and had the other
riverlords swear him fealty as their new liege.

00:11:54.349 --> 00:12:01.200
For centuries, House Hoare had terrorized
the Riverlands. Under House Tully, the Riverlands

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:07.320
would, at last, return to peace and prosperity.
After the castle cooled enough to allow men

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:11.829
inside, Aegon ventured into the ruin he had
made of Harrenhal.

00:12:11.829 --> 00:12:18.089
He saw the ashen bodies, the scorched stone,
and the mangled and melted swords of his former

00:12:18.089 --> 00:12:23.680
enemies. To his men's confusion, he ordered
these useless swords collected and sent to

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.270
his Aegonfort.

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:33.830
Varys: While Aegon marched on Harrenhal after
his coronation, Orys Baratheon had taken most

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:38.620
of his forces, and his queen Rhaenys with
her dragon, south to deal with the excuse

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:44.010
for the invasion: Argilac the Arrogant, King
of the Stormlands.

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:49.000
Argilac had his seat at Storm's End, a castle
considered the most impregnable in Westeros

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:55.460
after Harrenhal. Argilac may have been arrogant,
but he wasn't stupid or a coward. His lords

00:12:55.460 --> 00:13:00.730
advised him to shut his gates and wait out
the siege, but he'd heard what had happened

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:06.360
at Harrenhal and refused to die a suckling
pig cooked in his own castle. He would meet

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:13.010
victory or defeat the same way, with sword
in hand. He called his banners and marched

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:16.219
to meet Orys Baratheon in the field.

00:13:16.219 --> 00:13:22.659
Thanks to Rhaenys' dragon, Meraxes, Orys knew
Argilac was coming, how many men he had, and

00:13:22.659 --> 00:13:27.750
how fast he marched. So Orys simply seized
the high ground and dug in on the hills to

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:34.130
wait for Argilac. As the two armies approached,
the wind rose to meet them, and the rain poured

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:41.140
from the sky, a gale which would give the
battle its name: the Last Storm. King Argilac's

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:46.560
lords urged him to wait for the weather to
die down, but the Storm King saw that the

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:52.550
rain was blowing into the faces of the Baratheon
men on their hills and Argilac outnumbered

00:13:52.550 --> 00:14:02.110
the Baratheon host two to one, with four times
as many knights and heavy horse. Argilac attacked.

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:07.589
Three times Argilac led his knights against
the Baratheon line, but the hills were steep,

00:14:07.589 --> 00:14:15.240
and the rain had beat the earth mud. The warhorses
foundered and slipped, and the chargers collapsed.

00:14:15.240 --> 00:14:21.339
The battle seemed lost until Argilac ordered
the spearmen up the hill. Blinded by the rain,

00:14:21.339 --> 00:14:27.219
the Baratheons didn't see them until it was
too late. One hill fell, then another and

00:14:27.219 --> 00:14:34.810
another until only one remained in the Baratheon
center. If Argilac could break through there,

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.740
he could split the invading army and flank
both halves.

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:46.800
Argilac and his men charged, and the Baratheon
line broke, revealing Queen Rhaenys and Meraxes.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:52.630
Argilac's vanguard burst into flame, and his
men panicked. The victory charge fell into

00:14:52.630 --> 00:14:59.019
chaos, and Argilac himself was thrown from
his horse. But he didn't yield. When Orys

00:14:59.019 --> 00:15:05.090
Baratheon arrived, he found the old king holding
off half-a-dozen men, another half-dozen dead

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:11.690
at his feet. Orys dismounted to meet the king
on equal footing and offered Argilac one final

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:18.949
chance to yield. Argilac cursed him instead.
As the storm raged around them, the grizzled

00:15:18.949 --> 00:15:26.030
old warrior and the bearded upstart fought
for life and kingdom. In the end, Argilac

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:31.070
got his wish. He died, sword in hand.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:37.509
As word of Argilac's death spread, his lords
and knights threw down their swords and fled.

00:15:37.509 --> 00:15:42.640
Orys and his vanguard rode to Storm's End
to claim Argilac's castle for Aegon, only

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:48.959
to find the gates barred and the walls manned.
Argilac's daughter had assumed his crown,

00:15:48.959 --> 00:15:53.620
and the new Storm Queen was as fond of yielding
as her father.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:59.760
She declared that Orys would win only bones,
blood, and ashes here. But her men were weaker

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:06.719
than her, and that night Orys found Argilac's
daughter delivered, gagged, chained, and naked

00:16:06.719 --> 00:16:13.089
to his camp. Argilac had refused to give Orys
her hand. Now, Orys could have any part of

00:16:13.089 --> 00:16:19.089
her he wished. But Orys unchained the girl,
wrapped his cloak around her, and poured her

00:16:19.089 --> 00:16:25.010
a glass of wine. He told her he would take
the arms, banner, and words of House Durrandon

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:29.970
to honor her father's courage in the Last
Storm. Conveniently, Orys had none of his

00:16:29.970 --> 00:16:32.320
own to discard first.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:38.880
The crowned stag became the sigil of House
Baratheon, and Storm's End their seat. Argilac's

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:45.589
daughter would even remain in her home, though,
as a lady instead of a princess. The Stormlands

00:16:45.589 --> 00:16:52.779
were now Aegon's, and as tribute, Aegon demanded
the swords of the men Orys had defeated. For

00:16:52.779 --> 00:17:01.950
what purpose, Orys didn't know.
Jaime Lannister: Aegon now ruled two of the

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:07.191
Seven Kingdoms, but he would no longer be
able to take the rest piecemeal. For the first

00:17:07.191 --> 00:17:12.440
time in thousands of years, the kings put
aside their squabbles and joined forces against

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:14.000
a common enemy.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:18.241
My ancestor, King Loren of House Lannister,
was head of the wealthiest family in the Seven

00:17:18.241 --> 00:17:23.690
Kingdoms. When King Loren joined his forces
to Mern of House Gardener, King of the Reach,

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:30.710
they had the mightiest army in history, a
so-called iron fist to break the would-be

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:31.710
conqueror.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:36.610
But while an iron fist can smash a man's face
in battle, you'd look silly hunting birds

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:41.830
or beasts with it, and Aegon had a creature
that was both.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:46.400
The kings had never even seen a dragon, let
alone fought one. They had fought each other

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:51.000
for thousands of years, and victory always
went to the larger army.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:57.540
Surely a force five times that of Aegon's
could manage one dragon. But Aegon arrived

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:58.930
with three.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:04.330
Still, the Lannisters and Gardeners hoped
for victory. The battlefield they chose was

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:09.840
a wide plain with firm ground and clear skies.
Perfect for archers and mounted cavalry.

00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:15.100
But neither of the kings spared a thought
for why the ground was firm. There had been

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:19.090
no rain for a fortnight, which meant all the
wheat and grass on it were bone-dry. Perfect

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:20.090
for dragons.

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:27.320
At first, the kings looked like they would
emerge victorious. When the horn blew for

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:31.520
battle, their armies swept around Aegon's
flanks, and their iron fist of mounted knights

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:36.910
smashed through his center before the dragons
could even enter the fray. But then Aegon

00:18:36.910 --> 00:18:41.420
and his sisters took flight and unleashed
their dragons, not on the soldiers, but on

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:43.960
the dry fields all around them.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:52.110
The iron fist unclenched and became a hand
outstretched for mercy. As Aegon promised,

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.250
he had none.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:59.320
More than four thousand men died in the fires,
another thousand escaping them. Tens of thousands

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:03.500
returned home as monsters, burned and scarred
beyond recognition.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:09.000
House Gardener never returned at all. The
Field of Fire, as the singers call it, claimed

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:14.030
the last of the Gardener line, and House Tyrell
rose in their stead as Lords of the Reach

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:16.080
and Wardens of the South.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:21.330
As for my illustrious ancestor, when King
Loren saw the battle was lost, he rode through

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:27.080
a wall of flame and smoke to safety. Or at
least to a heroic capture a day later, where

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:30.270
he lay his sword before Aegon and knelt.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:35.890
Aegon, true to his word, spared him and confirmed
House Lannister as Lords of Casterly Rock

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:42.450
and Wardens of the West. Why wouldn't he?
A Lannister always pays his debts, and now

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:49.970
we owed our lives to the crown. That was worth
centuries of subservience, at least. Besides,

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:53.040
Aegon had a fetish for collecting swords,
not heads.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:58.190
He added Loren's to the pile his men had retrieved
from the Field of Fire and sent them back

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:06.320
to the Aegonfort.
Sansa Stark: With most of the South in Aegon's

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:11.490
hands, the best chance to throw back the Conqueror
now lay with the North, if we cared enough

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:13.420
to try.

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:17.520
Unlike our southern rivals, the Stark Kings
of Winter didn't forge the North into one

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:24.090
kingdom for glory or gold (there is little
of either here), but to survive.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:30.270
Alone in Westeros, the North remembered when
worse than dragons lay waste to armies.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:36.220
Thousands of years ago, the sun set on the
realms of men, and the Long Night began. A

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:41.410
new race emerged from the ice and snow: the
White Walkers. They demanded no crown, offered

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:45.820
no terms, spared no life, and the dead marched
with them.

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:51.850
With humanity facing extinction, a Stark sought
out the Children of the Forest, the most ancient

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:56.940
beings in Westeros, and convinced them to
ally with the men they'd once fought.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:21:02.370
Together, the two races pushed the Walkers
back into the Land of Always Winter and sealed

00:21:02.370 --> 00:21:08.770
it off from the Seven Kingdoms with the Wall,
three hundred miles of ice, stone, and earth

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:10.940
rising nearly seven hundred feet tall.

00:21:10.940 --> 00:21:16.580
To guard it, they established the Night's
Watch, a brotherhood sworn to defend the living

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:20.340
from the dead, whose vows erase both titles
and crimes.

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:26.280
Viserys Targaryen: After the Long Night, the
North tried to forget it belonged to a continent.

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:32.190
Perhaps through pride, perhaps through sheer
ignorance. You never can tell with the North.

00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:38.530
But as news of Aegon's dragons spread, Torrhen
Stark, the King of Winter, knew he couldn't

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:44.990
forget Westeros any longer and summoned his
lords to Winterfell. Many fools shrugged off

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:51.350
the threat while the rest placed wages on
how long the South would take to burn. Torrhen

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:57.360
silenced them with a command to assemble their
armies and descend from the North in force.

00:21:57.360 --> 00:22:02.680
Sansa: As the kings of the Rock and the Reach
burned on the Field of Fire, the greatest

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:06.710
Northern force since the Long Night crossed
the Neck into the Riverlands.

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:12.770
But when King Torrhen arrived at the Trident,
he saw on the opposing riverbank the combined

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:20.040
strength of all Aegon's conquered kingdoms.
A force larger than Torrhen's own by half,

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:21.960
and with three dragons.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:27.650
Viserys: That night, King Torrhen called a
conference of all his lords and advisors.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:34.480
Some wanted to fight and trust Northern valor
to carry the day (and burn on the Trident).

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:39.710
The wisest of them wanted to withdraw to Moat
Cailin, the fortress which had thrown back

00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:43.590
every southern invasion (and burn there).

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:50.180
One suicidal lord even wanted to ambush Aegon's
camp in the dark and kill the dragons as they

00:22:50.180 --> 00:22:53.190
slept or at the very least, their riders.

00:22:53.190 --> 00:23:01.431
Hard to tell what would have been his fate.
Burning? Beheading? Dismemberment? Perhaps

00:23:01.431 --> 00:23:02.470
all three.

00:23:02.470 --> 00:23:07.420
Sansa: My ancestor listened to their counsel,
and, in the morning, crossed the Trident under

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:09.320
a flag of parley.

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:14.520
Then King Torrhen of House Stark laid his
ancient crown at Aegon's feet and was named

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:18.000
Lord of Winterfell and Warden of the North.

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:20.280
Viserys: And the King Who Knelt.

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:25.890
Sansa: He had no choice, and thanks to him,
our soldiers returned to their homes whole

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:33.000
and unharmed. The swords that Aegon took from
them were not twisted, burnt, or mangled.

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:34.630
Viserys: Yet.

00:23:34.630 --> 00:23:42.400
Petyr Baelish: The Vale of Arryn was the last
of the great kingdoms left. Old and proud,

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:47.940
House Arryn did what they always did in times
of strife: they shut the Bloody Gate, sealing

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:49.490
off the Vale.

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:55.830
Then, the Queen Regent Sharra of House Arryn
retreated with her son, the boy-king Ronnel,

00:23:55.830 --> 00:24:01.480
into the Eyrie, their family's impregnable
fortress. From the top of their mountain,

00:24:01.480 --> 00:24:07.660
they could look down on Westeros far below,
its problems hidden beneath the clouds.

00:24:07.660 --> 00:24:12.490
But one day, Queen Sharra entered the outer
courtyard to find her young son sitting on

00:24:12.490 --> 00:24:18.670
the knee of Visenya Targaryen and ogling her
dragon, Vhagar, beside her. Just as he asked

00:24:18.670 --> 00:24:25.000
for another cake at dinner, little King Ronnel
asked his mother if he could ride on the nice

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:32.760
lady's dragon. Visenya smiled at Sharra. So,
Sharra imagined, did Vhagar.

00:24:32.760 --> 00:24:37.650
Remembering her manners, Sharra asked if she
could have Visenya brought some wine or food,

00:24:37.650 --> 00:24:43.400
she must be tired after such a long flight.
But Visenya demurred.

00:24:43.400 --> 00:24:49.750
Bored with his mother's pleasantries, Ronnel
demanded an answer. Poor boy. He didn't even

00:24:49.750 --> 00:24:57.240
understand the question. Sharra hesitated
for a moment, then asked Visenya, as a mother,

00:24:57.240 --> 00:25:04.800
if it was safe for the boy. Visenya assured
her it was. What choice did Sharra have?

00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:11.280
Whilst her son circled the castle, she collected
his little ringlet, her own regent's coronet,

00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:16.300
and the ancient Falcon Crown of Mountain and
Vale, which the Arryns had worn for thousands

00:25:16.300 --> 00:25:18.240
of years.

00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:24.030
Ronnel had taken to the sky as a king, but
he landed as a lordling. Perhaps he considered

00:25:24.030 --> 00:25:29.740
his ancient rights a fair trade for a few
minutes of flight, as a little boy would.

00:25:29.740 --> 00:25:36.050
More likely, he didn't even notice the three
crowns at Visenya's feet or recognize the

00:25:36.050 --> 00:25:44.830
swords of his garrison beside them.
Viserys Targaryen: The heads of Westeros had

00:25:44.830 --> 00:25:53.580
bowed to Aegon, but its heart still beat free.
Oldtown, the center of the Faith of the Seven.

00:25:53.580 --> 00:25:58.960
There dwelt the High Septon, the father of
the faithful, who commanded the obedience

00:25:58.960 --> 00:26:04.910
of all Westeros, save the savages of the North
and their Old Gods.

00:26:04.910 --> 00:26:10.110
When Aegon had landed in Westeros, the High
Septon had locked himself in the Starry Sept

00:26:10.110 --> 00:26:16.330
and fasted for seven days and seven nights,
one for each of his gods. All he received

00:26:16.330 --> 00:26:22.830
for his trouble was the divine wisdom that
if Oldtown took up arms against the dragon,

00:26:22.830 --> 00:26:27.470
the city would burn, faithful and faithless
alike.

00:26:27.470 --> 00:26:32.870
After the submission of House Stark, Aegon
marches towards Oldtown, steeling himself

00:26:32.870 --> 00:26:39.880
for another battle. But he found the gates
open, with the High Septon welcoming him.

00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:45.620
The pious fool even had the arrogance to grant
what Aegon had already won, and anointed the

00:26:45.620 --> 00:26:52.390
last Valyrian as "Aegon of House Targaryen,
First of His Name, King of the Andals and

00:26:52.390 --> 00:26:58.760
the First Men, Lord of the Seven Kingdoms
and Protector of the Realm." As if titles

00:26:58.760 --> 00:27:04.860
meant anything to a man to whom time itself
now bowed. The Maesters would hence divide

00:27:04.860 --> 00:27:10.780
all history into Before and After Conquest.

00:27:10.780 --> 00:27:17.611
Most expected Aegon to stay and make Oldtown
his seat, but soon after his coronation, Aegon

00:27:17.611 --> 00:27:23.990
returned to the mouth of the Blackwater River,
where he had first set foot on Westeros. A

00:27:23.990 --> 00:27:30.460
small town had since sprouted around his primitive
fort. To honor their new master, the locals

00:27:30.460 --> 00:27:36.550
dubbed it "King's Landing," though it looked
more fit for a hedge knight, with wooden palisades,

00:27:36.550 --> 00:27:43.300
muddy streets, and piles of mangled swords
carted in from every corner of the conquest.

00:27:43.300 --> 00:27:50.270
But when Aegon made it his court, wood became
stone, black mud was buried beneath a Red

00:27:50.270 --> 00:27:56.610
Keep, and the collected swords of Aegon's
foes were blasted by dragon fire and became

00:27:56.610 --> 00:28:05.150
a seat fit for the Conqueror and the greatest
dynasty this world has ever known. House Targaryen.

00:28:05.150 --> 00:28:14.700
My family. My throne. Or so it should have
been.

00:28:14.700 --> 00:28:21.410
Varys: But while Aegon titled himself Lord
of the Seven Kingdoms, in reality, he held

00:28:21.410 --> 00:28:29.270
only six. The seventh, Dorne, had never knelt.
Visenya had flown into the Vale and returned

00:28:29.270 --> 00:28:35.030
with its crown. Mimicking her sister, Rhaenys
had flown over the enemy force holding the

00:28:35.030 --> 00:28:40.180
passes into Dorne and landed in the castle
of its ruling lady, Princess Meria of House

00:28:40.180 --> 00:28:41.970
Martell.

00:28:41.970 --> 00:28:48.220
Meria was eighty years old, fat, bald, and
blind. Behind her back, many sniggered at

00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:53.400
her as the "Yellow Toad of Dorne." The beautiful
Rhaenys probably thought as much when they

00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:58.420
met. She demanded Princess Meria kneel to
her brother Aegon, though she allowed that

00:28:58.420 --> 00:29:03.760
on account of Meria's age and health, a simple
vow of submission would do.

00:29:03.760 --> 00:29:08.980
But the princess told the queen that the Targaryens
weren't wanted in Dorne, and no Martell would

00:29:08.980 --> 00:29:14.420
ever bow, bend or break no matter how badly
they burned. Rhaenys could have mounted her

00:29:14.420 --> 00:29:20.170
dragon right then, and roasted Meria in the
castle as her brother had done at Harrenhal.

00:29:20.170 --> 00:29:25.990
But whatever she saw in Meria's eyes scared
her right back to King's Landing, with a dragon's

00:29:25.990 --> 00:29:28.870
tail between its legs.

00:29:28.870 --> 00:29:35.490
After Aegon's coronation, Rhaenys returned
to Dorne with Aegon and Visenya and their

00:29:35.490 --> 00:29:41.200
dragons. But no armies met them in the field,
and no lords defied them in their castles.

00:29:41.200 --> 00:29:48.280
As the dragons approached, Dorne simply emptied.
House Martell had learned from Harrenhal and

00:29:48.280 --> 00:29:54.620
the Field of Fire. The dragons were unbeatable
in battle, but wars were more than battles.

00:29:54.620 --> 00:30:00.160
Unopposed, Aegon claimed Dorne for his own.
But as soon as he returned to King's Landing,

00:30:00.160 --> 00:30:05.340
his castellans were hurled off towers, and
his royal garrison vanished in the desert,

00:30:05.340 --> 00:30:11.140
never to be seen again. Except, perhaps, when
the winds change and the sands cough up old

00:30:11.140 --> 00:30:19.540
bones and armor. Rhaenys returned on Meraxes,
intent on avenging herself against Meria Martell.

00:30:19.540 --> 00:30:26.060
But Dorne was no longer empty. The Dornish
kept Meria's promise and fought even while

00:30:26.060 --> 00:30:30.510
burning under dragon flame. And they won.

00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:35.740
One day a bolt pierced the eye of Meraxes
and knocked the dragon out of the sky. House

00:30:35.740 --> 00:30:43.080
Martell remained unbroken, unlike the unfortunate
Rhaenys. In their wrath, Aegon and Visenya

00:30:43.080 --> 00:30:49.080
set flame to every castle and city but Sunspear,
trying to turn the people against House Martell.

00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:55.470
But the Dornish stayed loyal, and when Aegon
returned to King's Landing, he found assassins

00:30:55.470 --> 00:30:58.460
waiting for him in the streets of his own
capital.

00:30:58.460 --> 00:31:03.770
If not for Visenya, the Conqueror would not
have enjoyed his conquest for very long. From

00:31:03.770 --> 00:31:08.550
then on, the king and his family would be
guarded by the seven greatest knights in the

00:31:08.550 --> 00:31:11.880
realm: the Kingsguard.

00:31:11.880 --> 00:31:19.000
When Meria died in her sleep, a weak and tired
son sued for peace. But old Meria had exhausted

00:31:19.000 --> 00:31:25.260
Aegon as well, and he granted the request.
The Targaryens still wanted Dorne, and eventually,

00:31:25.260 --> 00:31:30.200
they would have it, but not at the point of
a sword. They would buy it the same way great

00:31:30.200 --> 00:31:37.360
lords buy anything: with a daughter.
Viserys Targaryen: After the Conquest, when

00:31:37.360 --> 00:31:44.270
men looked up, they saw dragons. Nobles learned
to keep their eyes down, but the gods weren't

00:31:44.270 --> 00:31:46.590
used to sharing the heavens.

00:31:46.590 --> 00:31:51.970
When Aegon died, the High Septon led the Faith
and its army in revolt, claiming that the

00:31:51.970 --> 00:31:57.080
Valyrian tradition of wedding brother to sister
was an abomination in the eyes of the Seven.

00:31:57.080 --> 00:32:02.380
Though no one could explain where the divine
Mother and Father had come from.

00:32:02.380 --> 00:32:09.130
My ancestor Maegor the Wise, or Maegor the
Cruel as men slander him, put a bounty on

00:32:09.130 --> 00:32:16.050
the head of every militant priest, and miraculously
the Faith soon returned to the septs.

00:32:16.050 --> 00:32:21.300
With Dorne in the fold, and the Faith put
in its place, none in Westeros were left to

00:32:21.300 --> 00:32:25.160
oppose my family, so we started opposing each
other.

00:32:25.160 --> 00:32:31.401
In a Dance of Dragons, a Targaryen princess
tried to steal her brother's throne. Thanks

00:32:31.401 --> 00:32:38.610
to her stupidity, most of our dragons died,
though one thankfully ate her before it did.

00:32:38.610 --> 00:32:44.570
But even without our dragons, we were still
the blood of Old Valyria, which proved just

00:32:44.570 --> 00:32:46.110
as dangerous.

00:32:51.302 --> 00:32:54.282
and legitimized them all on his deathbed.

00:32:58.907 --> 00:33:04.537
father's kingdom. And when they failed, their
sons tried. When their sons failed, their

00:33:04.537 --> 00:33:06.267
grandsons tried.

00:33:06.267 --> 00:33:11.437
Until finally, Ser Barristan the Bold, Knight
of the Kingsguard, slew Maelys the Monstrous

00:33:11.437 --> 00:33:16.617
in the War of the Ninepenny Kings, ending
the last of the Blackfyre line.

00:33:16.617 --> 00:33:22.497
Ultimately, without our dragons and with our
blood diluted by commoners, we failed to see

00:33:22.497 --> 00:33:24.787
the greatest threat growing under our noses.

